## 1. Summary

- **Question:** with a limited retention budget, which customers should receive an offer when both churn risk and economic value count?
- **Answer:** rank customers by expected net value of an offer (p(churn) x save rate x value - cost), let an optimiser pick the customer-offer combination within budget, and size the budget where the marginal return falls below {{ recommendation.hurdle_marginal_roi | pct(0) }}.
- **Who:** the recommended list is {{ profile.by['InternetService|Fiber optic'].list_share | pct(0) }} fibre and {{ profile.by['Contract|Month-to-month'].list_share | pct(0) }} month-to-month customers with a median bill of {{ profile.list.median_monthly_charges | usd }} ({{ profile.all.median_monthly_charges | usd }} overall); low-risk customers and risky customers with small bills get no offer.
- **Impact (test split, same {{ budget.base | usd }} budget):** {{ strategy_label | lower }} {{ chosen.expected_net_value | usd }} vs {{ c.risk.expected_net_value | usd }} for risk-only targeting, **{{ headline.delta_vs_risk | signed_usd }}** ({{ headline.targeting_effect | usd }} from targeting, {{ headline.offer_design_effect | usd }} from offer design); valued with actual churn {{ headline.gain_label.label_based_simulated_net | signed_usd }} (95% interval {{ headline.gain_label.lower_95 | usd }} to {{ headline.gain_label.upper_95 | usd }}).
- **Budget:** {{ budget.recommended_per_base_customer | usd(2) }} per customer in the base (enough for the standard offer to {{ recommendation.recommended_share | pct(0) }} of customers; validation rule) buys {{ recommended.selected_count | num }} offers on test ({{ recommended.contacted_share | pct(0) }} of customers) for {{ recommended.cost | usd }} and {{ recommended.expected_net_value | usd }} expected net value.
- **Main risk:** the save rate is assumed. Break-even {{ be.break_even_default_save_rate | pct }} for the base-budget list and {{ recommended.break_even.break_even_default_save_rate | pct }} for the recommended list (standard-offer save rate), vs assumed {{ default_offer.save_rate | pct(0) }}; with all assumptions uncertain the recommended list loses money in {{ monte_carlo.by.recommended.prob_loss | pct(0) }} of draws. A randomised pilot measures the save rate before scale-up.
- **Outside the sample:** at {{ stress.targets[0] | pct(0) }} average churn only {{ stress.by['sample|' ~ ('%g' % stress.targets[0])].positive_ev_share | pct(0) }} of customers would be worth the standard offer; only {{ reasons.addressable_share | pct(0) }} of churners left for reasons an offer can address.

